# Environment variables
#
# frontend/.env is currently TRACKED on purpose - it holds only VITE_* values
# (API base URL, OAuth client ids) that are compiled into the browser bundle and
# are public by definition. These rules stop anything else landing in the repo:
# this is a public repository, and a secret added to a .env here would be
# committed by the next `git add -A` with nothing to catch it.
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.production
.env.development
